Low Density Housing - Addition / Alteration - To permit exterior and interior alterations to this existing one family dwelling plus built in three car garage by adding a covered sundeck at the rear on the second floor with a roof-cover and over a existing roof deck at the rear; remove concrete throughout the site to achieve 70% impermeability; and change the use to add a secondary suite on the main floor to this inside with lane site as heard by the Board of Variance approval Z35020 dated on December 14th 2016 thereby granting a relaxation of the Floor Space Ratio subject to the following conditions:

(1) That all exterior decks and balconies must remain open(uncovered) and shall never be enclosed and/or covered at anytime in the future;

(2) That the site must be in compliance with the Site Impermeability regulations of 0.70(or 70%) in accordance with the Board's decision on November 10th 2015;

(3) That a portion of the front yard driveway ( the right-hand side of the driveway) must be removed in order to be in compliance with the .70 (or 70%) Site Impermeability regulations of the RS-1 District Schedule;

(4) That the existing attached one car garage must be maintained for parking use only (and used as non-habitable space) and cannot be converted into living space or habitable area at anytime in the future.

Addressing Note: 

Principle dwelling 5894 Lincoln Street 
Secondary suite  5896 Lincoln Street 
Note: 3'-0" continuous pathway for firefighter access to secondary suite to be maintained at all times.

